@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@contentType = application/json

### ============================================================
### Lab04 zadanie 4 — tabela uprawnień (logi / screenshoty)
### Wymaga: npm run seed:run && npm start
### Konta seed:
###   ADMIN  admin@example.com / admin-super-secret-password
###   OWNER  anna.nowak@example.com / seed-user-password-xx  (rezerwacja id=2)
###   OTHER  jan.kowalski@example.com / seed-user-password-xx
### Kolumny: brak tokenu | USER właściciel | USER obcy | ADMIN
### ============================================================

### --- Logowania (uruchom najpierw, żeby ustawić tokeny) ---

### Login ADMIN
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "admin-super-secret-password"
}

###
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login USER właściciel (Anna — reservations/:id = 2)
# @name loginOwner
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "anna.nowak@example.com",
  "password": "seed-user-password-xx"
}

###
@ownerToken = {{loginOwner.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login USER obcy (Jan)
# @name loginOther
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "jan.kowalski@example.com",
  "password": "seed-user-password-xx"
}

###
@otherToken = {{loginOther.response.body.accessToken}}

### ============================================================
### GET /api/buildings → 401 | 200 | 200 | 200
### ============================================================

### GET /api/buildings — brak tokenu → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings

### GET /api/buildings — USER właściciel → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### GET /api/buildings — USER obcy → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### GET /api/buildings — ADMIN → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ============================================================
### POST /api/buildings → 401 | 403 | 403 | 201
### ============================================================

### POST /api/buildings — brak tokenu → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Budynek Test Brak",
  "address": "ul. Test 1"
}

### POST /api/buildings — USER właściciel → 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Budynek Test Owner",
  "address": "ul. Test 2"
}

### POST /api/buildings — USER obcy → 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Budynek Test Other",
  "address": "ul. Test 3"
}

### POST /api/buildings — ADMIN → 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Budynek Test Admin",
  "address": "ul. Test 4"
}

### ============================================================
### POST /api/rooms → 401 | 403 | 403 | 201
### ============================================================

### POST /api/rooms — brak tokenu → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "buildingId": 1,
  "name": "R-brak",
  "capacity": 5
}

### POST /api/rooms — USER właściciel → 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "buildingId": 1,
  "name": "R-owner",
  "capacity": 5
}

### POST /api/rooms — USER obcy → 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "buildingId": 1,
  "name": "R-other",
  "capacity": 5
}

### POST /api/rooms — ADMIN → 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "buildingId": 1,
  "name": "R-admin",
  "capacity": 5
}

### ============================================================
### GET /api/reservations → 401 | 200 (swoje) | 200 (swoje) | 200 (wszystkie)
### ============================================================

### GET /api/reservations — brak tokenu → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?limit=1

### GET /api/reservations — USER właściciel → 200 (tylko userId=3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### GET /api/reservations — USER obcy → 200 (tylko userId=4)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### GET /api/reservations — ADMIN → 200 (wszystkie)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ============================================================
### GET /api/reservations?userId=3 → 401 | 403 | 403 | 200
### ============================================================

### GET /api/reservations?userId=3 — brak tokenu → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?userId=3

### GET /api/reservations?userId=3 — USER właściciel → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?userId=3
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### GET /api/reservations?userId=3 — USER obcy → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?userId=3
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### GET /api/reservations?userId=3 — ADMIN → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?userId=3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ============================================================
### GET /api/reservations/2 → 401 | 200 | 404 | 200
### (id=2 należy do Anny / OWNER)
### ============================================================

### GET /api/reservations/2 — brak tokenu → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/2

### GET /api/reservations/2 — USER właściciel → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/2
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### GET /api/reservations/2 — USER obcy → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/2
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### GET /api/reservations/2 — ADMIN → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ============================================================
### PATCH /api/reservations/:id/cancel → 401 | 200* | 404 | 200*/409
### * 409 gdy rezerwacja już rozpoczęta (np. id=1)
### Używamy przyszłej rezerwacji Anny (id=2) do cancel OWNER/ADMIN
### oraz id=2 dla OTHER → 404; id=1 dla ADMIN → 409 (started)
### ============================================================

### PATCH cancel/2 — brak tokenu → 401
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/2/cancel

### PATCH cancel/2 — USER obcy → 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/2/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### PATCH cancel/1 — ADMIN (już rozpoczęta) → 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### PATCH cancel/2 — USER właściciel → 200
### (uruchom po wierszach powyżej; po cancel status=CANCELLED)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/2/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### --- Opcjonalnie: świeża rezerwacja + cancel ADMIN ---

### ADMIN tworzy rezerwację do cancel
# @name adminCreateReservation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "roomId": 5,
  "participants": 2,
  "startTime": "2027-09-01T10:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2027-09-01T11:00:00.000Z"
}

###
@adminReservationId = {{adminCreateReservation.response.body.id}}

### PATCH cancel (ADMIN, przyszła) → 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/{{adminReservationId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
